# Deferred: stale app.js after deploy (build stamp)

Soft-nav keeps the in-memory `app.js`. It already reloads when the script `src` `?v=` changes (`loadUpdatedAppJs`), but today that string is tied to static `APP_VERSION` (`0.4.0`), so after `./pull-restart.ps1` a hard refresh is often still required.

## Later idea (not implemented) — option 1

Put a **deploy/build stamp** in the `/client/app.js?v=…` URL (content hash of `app.js`, git short hash, or file mtime) so every deploy changes `src`. Soft-nav’s existing compare then swaps the script without a hard reload.

### Do not

- Add a freshness fetch on the Creo **Connecting** path (must not slow connect)
- Poll `/client/app.js` before Creo.JS is Connected
- Block boot waiting on a build-id round-trip

### Preferred shape

- Stamp baked into HTML at process start / template render
- Detection only on soft-nav (HTML already fetched) or idle/focus later — never during connect overlay
